hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27901","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they both said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from his grandmother Umm Hakim, from her sister Dubaah bint al-Zubayr, that she offered meat to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he nibbled from it, then he prayed and did not perform ablution. My father said: Affan said: She offered meat to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"27902","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Dubaah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Enter ihram and say: My release is where You detain me, for if I am detained or fall ill, I have thereby become lawful by that, your stipulation upon your Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"27903","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: Al-Awzai narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, he said: One who heard Ibn Abbas narrated to me, saying: Dubaah narrated to me that she said: O Messenger of Allah, I intend Hajj. He said to her: Perform Hajj and stipulate."
